  "result": "I've written the 30-minute lesson on context and memory, plus a short quiz, an answer key and a cheat sheet. I couldn't run a word count in this environment (the shell blocked the scripts I tried). I added a section after my first draft to reach the length, but I don't know whether it lands near 30 minutes.\n\n- **Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory-in-an-agent.html`\n  - It covers the context window, what the program keeps between steps, trimming a full context, notes between sessions, and retrieval for finding the right manual page.\n  - Each part has a worked example from the makerspace assistant, with token counts.\n  - There are three figures and a practice check in most sections, and it ends with a memory plan for the assistant.\n  - The primary source is Anthropic's [Effective context engineering for AI agents](https://anthropic.com/engineering/effective-context-engineering-for-ai-agents). I fetched and read it. For the other two sources I only read search snippets, plus a partial read of the arXiv survey (its last ~15,000 characters were cut off), so their citations are thinner.\n- **Quiz:** `quizzes/0002.json` has five items. The answer key is in `keys/0002.json`.\n- **Also written:** `cheatsheets/context-and-memory.html`, a new `RESOURCES.md`, and an update to `NOTES.md`.\n\nI made up two misconception ids for the key because I couldn't tell whether they already exist: M7 (a bigger window means paste everything) and M8 (save everything, even live data). M3 (the model remembers by itself) comes from key 0001.\n\nQuiz 0001 has two ungraded submissions, so I didn't build on it. Ask for the quiz when you're ready, or ask me anything about the lesson.\n\nDo you want sub-agents next, or workflows versus agents? I left sub-agents out of this lesson on purpose.",
